<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="013" project="ai-advanced-capabilities-analysis-hub-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>File resolution via `sprk_documentid` → `sprk_document` SPE hop</title>
    <phase>1 Data spine</phase>
    <gate>blocked-until-011</gate>
    <status>completed</status>
    <rigor>STANDARD</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Wires file open/preview through the existing document lookup + SpeFileStore facade; reuses established SPE plumbing with a hard MUST-NOT (no pointer duplication) — modification of existing surface, STANDARD.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Applies the known ADR-007 document-hop pattern to the Analysis record; well-specified reuse, no architectural authoring — Sonnet-5 @ high.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>P1</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <deps>011</deps>
    <tags>frontend, spe</tags>
    <estimated-effort>2-3 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>
    Resolve an Analysis's files by hopping through its `sprk_documentid` → `sprk_document` lookup to the document's SPE
    pointers (per ADR-007), reusing the existing `SpeFileStore` server facade path. Do NOT duplicate
    `speDriveItemId` / `GraphDriveId` / `GraphItemId` onto `sprk_analysis`; the document record remains the single
    source of SPE addressing.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    SPAARKE platform developer. Expert in the SharePoint Embedded document hop (`sprk_documentid` → `sprk_document` →
    SPE pointers) and the `SpeFileStore` facade. Follow ADR-007 strictly.
  </role>

  <goal>
    File open/preview for a `sprk_analysis` resolves SPE pointers via the `sprk_documentid` → `sprk_document` lookup and
    the existing `SpeFileStore` path; no SPE pointer columns are added to `sprk_analysis`; the resolution is covered by
    a test asserting the document-hop is used (not a duplicated pointer on the Analysis record).
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      Per spec FR-04 / PLAN 1.3, analysis files are reached THROUGH the existing document lookup — the same SPE hop used
      across Spaarke — rather than by copying SPE pointers onto the Analysis. Owner confirms `sprk_documentid` is KEPT as
      the SPE subject-pointer (a separate role from `sprk_regardingdocument`). This consumes the client `sprk_analysis`
      type (011) and reuses the server `SpeFileStore` facade (ADR-007). No new SPE pointer columns are created (spec §11.4 / NFR-05).
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/Graph/SpeFileStore.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">src/solutions/SpaarkeAi/src/ (Analysis file open/preview → document-hop resolution)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">.claude/adr/ADR-007-spe-file-storage.md</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="011" status="pending">Client `sprk_analysis` type (with `sprk_documentid` lookup) exists.</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-007">SCOPE = Analysis file resolution. Files MUST be reached via `sprk_documentid` → `sprk_document` → the document's SPE pointers through the existing `SpeFileStore` facade; MUST NOT duplicate `speDriveItemId`/`GraphDriveId`/`GraphItemId` onto `sprk_analysis`.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">SCOPE = reuse the existing document-hop + `SpeFileStore` path; do NOT author a new SPE addressing service or a new BFF endpoint for this (extend/consume the existing path). `sprk_documentid` is the subject-pointer, distinct from `sprk_regardingdocument`.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-013">SCOPE = if any BFF-side call is needed, go through the existing facade/`PublicContracts` seams; MUST NOT fork `Services/Ai/` or inject AI-internal types.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>SharePoint Embedded document hop</topic>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-007-spe-file-storage.md</file>
      <file>.claude/patterns/ai/text-extraction.md</file>
      <file>docs/data-model/</file>
    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="SpeFileStore facade" location="src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/Graph/SpeFileStore.cs">
        The existing SPE addressing facade; resolve the document's pointers through it after the `sprk_documentid` → `sprk_document` lookup — do not re-address SPE from the Analysis record.
      </pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Declare STANDARD rigor + reason. Study the existing document-hop usage + `SpeFileStore` facade.</step>
    <step order="1">Implement Analysis file open/preview to read `sprk_analysis.sprk_documentid`, load the `sprk_document`, and resolve its SPE pointers via the existing facade path.</step>
    <step order="2">Confirm no SPE pointer field is read from or written to `sprk_analysis` (the type has none per 011; assert nothing reintroduces them).</step>
    <step order="3">Add a test asserting resolution goes through the document hop (given an Analysis with a `sprk_documentid`, the SPE pointer comes from the linked document, not the Analysis).</step>
    <step order="4">Build + run tests; confirm green. If a BFF-touching change was made, run the publish-size + CVE checks (spec NFR-01/NFR-06) and record them.</step>
    <step order="5">Update TASK-INDEX.md: set task 013 status to ✅.</step>
    <step order="6">Document any deviation in `projects/ai-advanced-capabilities-analysis-hub-r1/notes/`.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If reaching files through the document hop proves impossible without adding an SPE pointer to `sprk_analysis` (e.g. an Analysis with no `sprk_documentid`), STOP and escalate per CLAUDE.md §6.5 — do NOT silently duplicate SPE pointers onto the Analysis to work around it.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <ui-tests>
    <test name="Analysis file opens/previews via document hop (theme smoke)">
      <steps>
        <step>Open/preview a file for an Analysis whose `sprk_documentid` points to a document with SPE pointers.</step>
        <step>Toggle light → dark theme.</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>The file opens/previews correctly with the pointer resolved from the linked `sprk_document` (not from the Analysis). The preview surface renders correctly in dark mode (ADR-021: Fluent v9 tokens, no hard-coded colors).</expected>
    </test>
  </ui-tests>

  <tools>
    <tool name="npm">Build + run the SpaarkeAi client tests.</tool>
    <tool name="dotnet">Only if a BFF-side change is made: build + publish-size + CVE checks.</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/solutions/SpaarkeAi/src/ (Analysis file open/preview via document-hop resolution)</output>
    <output type="test">src/solutions/SpaarkeAi/src/ (test asserting SPE pointer resolves via the document lookup)</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a `sprk_analysis` with a `sprk_documentid`, when a file is opened/previewed, then the SPE pointer is resolved via the `sprk_documentid` → `sprk_document` hop through the existing `SpeFileStore` path.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: no SPE pointer column (`speDriveItemId`/`GraphDriveId`/`GraphItemId`) is read from or added to `sprk_analysis` (verify by grep/diff on the type + resolution code).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: given an Analysis with no `sprk_documentid`, file open surfaces a clear no-document state (not a fabricated pointer / unhandled error).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The resolution test passes; build is green (and, if BFF was touched, publish-size ≤60 MB + no new HIGH CVE recorded).</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>
    spec FR-04 / §11.4 / NFR-05 / ADR-007. `sprk_documentid` (SPE subject-pointer) is KEPT and is distinct from
    `sprk_regardingdocument` (regarding/context lookup handled in 012).

    COMPLETED 2026-07-28. Implemented as a standalone resolution module (no hub/reopen consumer exists yet at
    Phase 1 — those land in tasks 030/031) so later phases spread its output straight into
    `RichFilePreviewDialog`/`RichFilePreview` props:
      - `src/solutions/SpaarkeAi/src/services/analysisFileResolution.ts` — `resolveAnalysisDocumentId()` reads
        ONLY `_sprk_documentid_value` off `sprk_analysis` (the entire "hop" read); `resolveAnalysisFilePreview()`
        wires that id into the EXISTING BFF `GET /api/documents/{id}/preview-url` surface (SpeFileStore resolves
        the SPE pointer server-side) — the exact same call shape already shipped in this solution's
        `ConversationPane.tsx` FIX #7a (`fetchSavedPreviewUrl`), reused verbatim per CLAUDE.md §11 (no new BFF
        endpoint, no new SPE-addressing service, no `Services/Ai/` touch — ADR-013 N/A here since no AI call is
        made). Returns a discriminated union: `{status:'resolved', documentId, documentName, fetchPreviewUrl}` or
        `{status:'no-document'}` — the negative case (no `sprk_documentid`) is a first-class return value, not an
        escalation; the `<escalation>` trigger (duplicating a pointer onto the Analysis to work around a missing
        document) never fired because the existing document-preview BFF surface handles "no document" and
        "preview unavailable" gracefully already.
      - `src/solutions/SpaarkeAi/src/services/__tests__/analysisFileResolution.test.ts` — 9 tests (Jest): the
        document-hop id-read, the BFF call target being the LINKED `sprk_document` id, the no-document negative
        case, and 3 `fetchPreviewUrl` failure-mode cases (network error / non-ok response / no `bffBaseUrl`) all
        resolving to `null` rather than throwing.
      - No SPE pointer field (`speDriveItemId`/`GraphDriveId`/`GraphItemId`) is read from or added to
        `sprk_analysis` — verified by grep (only doc-comment prose references those names, explaining what is
        NOT duplicated) and by `sprkAnalysis.ts` (task 011, untouched — read-only import).
    Gates run: `npx tsc --noEmit` (SpaarkeAi solution) — zero errors attributable to the new files (pre-existing
    unrelated `@tiptap/*` module-resolution errors in `Spaarke.Compose.Components` predate this task and are
    out of scope); `npx jest src/services/__tests__/analysisFileResolution.test.ts` — 9/9 passed. BFF was NOT
    touched (no new endpoint/service), so publish-size/CVE checks are N/A. Step 9.5 quality gates skipped per
    STANDARD rigor (no override condition — not a test-modifying task per the CLAUDE.md §8 override row; the new
    test file is a task DELIVERABLE, not a modification to an existing `tests/**` KEEP-path file).
  </notes>

  <execution>
    <skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill>
    <protocol>Load knowledge files. Follow task-execute (STANDARD rigor; Step 9.5 gates skipped unless BFF touched).</protocol>
  </execution>
</task>
